          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"9-1\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_1\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The graph includes the stated business actions with acceptable paraphrase/abstraction: backup, initial table check, CRM checks, registration, possible report/table production and sending, reconciliation, and supervisor notifications.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"Required matched-action precedence is preserved: backup before initial check; the no-new-records path leads to CRM checking before registration/reporting; first-phase work leads to the 2:30 timing check; then the post-report CRM check precedes any reconciliation and the 4:00 timing check.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The candidate captures the main decisions and continuations: branching on new records, branching on new returns, conditional report sending based on advised codes, alert-if-late behavior at 2:30, and optional reconciliation with 4:00 escalation.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"none\",\"explanation\":\"Under the most defensible reading of the source, the generated graph preserves the intended process behavior: it models the weekday-morning backup and initial table check, the conditional no-new-records CRM/registration/reporting path, the 2:30 pm alert-if-late check, the subsequent CRM recheck after report completion, the optional reconciliation, and the 4:00 pm supervisor message if late. No clear missing business action, precedence reversal, or wrong branch/termination behavior is established from the source text. The only material issue is source ambiguity about whether the post-report CRM/reconciliation stage is intended to follow all first-phase outcomes or only cases where an actual new defaulting account report is produced; under the provisional reading adopted here, the graph is semantically preserved.\",\"overall_score\":1,\"severity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"ambiguity_flag\":true,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"The phrase 'Once the new defaulting account report has been completed' is materially ambiguous. It could mean the later CRM/reconciliation stage always follows completion of the first phase, or only follows cases where a new report/table is actually produced. The graph routes all first-phase outcomes into that later stage, and a different interpretation could change the diagnosis.\",\"requires_human_review\":true,\"review_reason\":\"Human review is needed to resolve whether the second CRM/reconciliation stage should occur after every first-phase outcome or only after actual report-production cases, which could change the control-flow diagnosis and score.\"}"
        }
